1.1.text:
Article 9
(1) Forms of protection services for women victims of violence include: a. legal aid services;
b. health services;
c. social rehabilitation services;
d. repatriation and social reintegration services;
e. complaint, consultation, and counseling services; and/or f. assistance services.
(2) Protection services for women as referred to in paragraph (1) include receiving and sending case referrals from or to other service units in a networked manner.
(3) Implementation of protection services for women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by Regional Apparatus having principal tasks and functions in the field of women's empowerment.
(4) Further provisions regarding the forms and procedures for protection services for women victims of violence shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

REGENT OF SLEMAN,

Considering : a. that in order to restore the dignity and honor of women and children victims of violence and to restore their social function, it is necessary to undertake efforts for protection, empowerment of women, and rehabilitation of child victims of violence;
b. that based on Article 12 of Law 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, empowerment of women and protection of children constitute mandatory governmental affairs for regional governments;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 15 of 1950 concerning Establishment of Regency Regions within the Special Region of Yogyakarta (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 44);
3. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606) as amended by Government Regulation in Lieu of Law of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1 of 2016 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);
4. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
5. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as last amended by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
6. Government Regulation Number 32 of 1950 concerning Determination of the Effective Date of Laws Number 12, 13, 14 and 15 concerning Establishment of Regency Regions in East/Central/West Java and the Special Region of Yogyakarta (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 59);
7. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);
8. Regional Regulation of the Special Region Province of Yogyakarta Number 3 of 2012 concerning Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence (Regional Gazette of the Special Region Province of Yogyakarta of 2012 Number 3, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of the Special Region Province of Yogyakarta of 2012 Number 3);
9. Regional Regulation of Sleman Regency Number 18 of 2013 concerning Implementation of Child Protection (Regional Gazette of Sleman Regency of 2013 Number 4 Series E, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Sleman Regency Number 79);

With Mutual Approval

CHAPTER IV
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 16
(1) Every Victim obtains the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity respected as a human being; b. the right to health and psychological recovery;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality of their identity;
f. the right to compensation from the perpetrator;
g. the right to social rehabilitation;
h. the right to complaint handling;
i. the right to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and/or
j. the right to assistance.
(2) Child victims of violence, in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in paragraph (1), also obtain the following special rights:
a. the right to respect for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and/or
e. the right to obtain freedom.

Article 3
The protection of women and children victims of violence is implemented based on the principles of:
a. gender responsiveness;
b. non-discrimination;
c. equal and respectful relationships;
d. maintaining privacy and confidentiality;
e. providing a sense of safety and comfort;
f. respecting individual differences;
g. non-judgmental;
h. respecting the choices and decisions of victims;
i. sensitivity to the background and condition of victims;
j. use of language that is appropriate and understood by victims; k. fast and simple;
l. empathy; and
m. best interests of victims.

